<item>
            <title>[MAHOUT-1577] FindBugs and PMD settings unrealistic </title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MAHOUT-1577</link>
                <project id="12310751" key="MAHOUT">Mahout</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;We get warnings on every use of a non-final method in a constructor.  This is arguably slightly risky, but I haven&apos;t ever seen a bug from this.  Similarly, we haven&apos;t had any problems with long methods (inherent in Hadoop programs, I think) nor with putting literals after variables in comparisons.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I am going to turn these warnings off to decrease noise levels.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
